    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "here's the text for section 4.2: \"4.2 Price Adjustments: SwiftRoute shall be entitled to fixed rates for the duration of the standard term. However, during peak demand months (June, July, August), the Supplier reserves the right to implement a price adjustment of up to 5% to account for market volatility. Such adjustments shall be applied to the upcoming billing cycle automatically.\" \n\nso basically, is there anything in there that lets them change the rates unexpectedly? i really need to be sure we're covered.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
